  "description": "Squeamishness aside, the tongue is such an appealing cut: tender and fatty, and delicate in taste (unlike kidneys or liver, for instance, which have a more distinctive flavor). I enjoy tongue sandwiches. Like corned beef or pastrami, the thin slices of tongue are so rich and satisfying that it's perfect between two slices of rye bread. All it needs is some horseradish and mustard, and maybe a dill pickle.",
  "notes": "Total time, including resting: 4 days 15 hr 10 min to 5 days 15 hr 10 min.\n\nOptional substitutions: calves tongue → beef tongue",
